HOTD4 (GROUP_HOD4), wrong 3D colours on Mesa: none of the game's standard material programs (fs/dat/std.dat0 + std.dat1)
links. The fragment shader always reads nnglvTexCoord01/23/45/67 and nnglvViewPositionFog, the vertex shader writes only the
ones the material uses; Mesa follows GLSL 1.10/1.20 and refuses the link ("fragment shader varying ... not written by vertex
shader"), NVIDIA accepts it. The game then draws every surface without its shader (raw base or normal maps: purple-blue walls,
purple/green surfaces in the first cutscene). Measured 2026-10-21: all 1599 programs compiled in a chapter 1 run fail to link
on Mesa; with these five varyings set to 0 at the start of the vertex shader's main() all 1599 link. The loader already routes
glShaderSourceARB through gl_ShaderSourceARB for every game; this adds the vertex-shader fix for GROUP_HOD4 only, and only when
the source is that standard vertex shader. HOTD4 itself was not routed through that interception: in Rev C its one
glXGetProcAddressARB call (0x081b6fb7) now goes to hod4GetProcAddressARB, which hands out the intercepted glShaderSourceARB
and passes every other name to the normal lookup. Applies after 0005 (both change patch.c).

